Package: acer-h340-usb-backup-dkms
Version: @VERSION@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ehsan Enaloo <19691857+ehsanenaloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: dkms
Recommends: linux-headers-amd64
Description: Acer H340 USB Backup button kernel module (DKMS)
 Turns the front USB Backup button of an Acer Aspire easyStore H340 into a
 Linux KEY_COPY input event. The module binds only the firmware's PNP0C32
 button node on this board, reads no ports and starts no copy.
 The module is built for the running kernel with DKMS and needs its headers.
 Loading it is left to the boot-time module list in /etc/modules-load.d.
